# A spiral-wound module refuses, by name, a present component it does not model
# (DEV.md 4c C188 defect 1).  Former gate: check_membrane_feed_scope.py.
# SpiralWoundModule carries the solvent (water) and the solutes the case declares
# `role nonvolatile;`.  Any OTHER present component was given z = 0 in both outlets
# and its mass re-counted as water: an ethanol feed came out with no ethanol, the
# kg balance closing and the carbon gone, at exit 0.  Witnesses are built from
# membrane01 (seawater RO, water + NaCl), its seal removed so the copy may change
# its component set.  (a) ethanol in the feed is refused naming the component and
# the remedy; (b) a feed without water is refused; (c) membrane01 still runs.
# NOT checked: the ethanol-as-solute route (held by the membrane goldens).
group      membrane-feed-scope
row        membrane-feed-scope
binary     choupoSolve
base       tutorials/steady/membranes/membrane01_RO_NaCl_seawater
strip      constant/propertyManifest expected
ok_head    "check_membrane_feed_scope: OK -- "
fail_head  "check_membrane_feed_scope: FAILED"
bullet     plain
ok_tail    .  NOT checked: the declared pass-through approximation (C188, not built)

probe      (a) ethanol in the feed
  edit     constant/thermoPhysPropDict	( water  NaCl )	( water  NaCl  ethanol )
  edit     0/feed	NaCl    5.98 kmol/h;	NaCl    5.98 kmol/h;\n    ethanol  5.0 kmol/h;
  match    'ethanol'
  match    does not model
  match    role nonvolatile
  match    B_s
  ok       an ethanol feed is refused naming the component and the remedy

probe      (b) no water
  edit     0/feed	re:water\s+569\.02 kmol/h;	water    0 kmol/h;
  match    carries no water
  ok       a water-free feed is refused for its missing solvent

control    (c) membrane01 itself
  ok       membrane01 (water + NaCl) runs as before
